  "name": "Question 17",
  "problem": "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's start by writing the matrix $A-\\lambda I:$\n\ufeff\ufeff\ufeff\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -\\sqrt{3})(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\lambda =2.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal.",
